cdk: unpin the frozen grab cursor when the pointer moves

The image that cursorless grabs freeze on the grab window is meant for
the repeated menu grabs of a held key: the toggling grabs would
otherwise show the theme's arrow while active and the cursor of the
window under the pointer while inactive, flickering at the key repeat
rate while the pointer sits still on, say, another application's text
box.

The frozen image outlives the churn, though: pressing the key once and
then moving the pointer keeps that image over the whole screen until the
grab ends, whatever window it passes, because the server shows the grab
window's cursor for every window outside the grabbed one.  It happens
whichever application the pointer sits on; the frozen image comes from
the grabbing client, not from the window under the pointer.

Let the first pointer movement under the grab unpin it: the pointer
proxy applies a NULL cursor on the grab window, which nothing else does
while the grab lasts, and the device swaps the frozen image for the
theme's default arrow there, remembering the arrow for the rest of the
grab so the windows applying their cursor during it stay consistent.
Grabs taken with an explicit cursor have no frozen image to unpin and
show that cursor regardless of the window attributes, so their grab
window is left untouched, and the request is a no-op for the grabs that
defined the arrow instead of freezing.
